  - name: CPU User Max
    detail: Mean User time has exceeded a 95% CPU threshold for over 5 mins
    calendar: OfficeHours
    fluxfile: flux/usage_user.flux
    severity: 1
    threshold: 95 
    comparison: gt
    tags: 
      - host
      - _field
      - _measurement
    interval: 300
    target: postfix
    action: | 
              An extended period of extremely high CPU User time indicates unusal activity or a defective process. VM metrics 
              can be used to ascertain if there is a sudden and unusal spike in such activity. Login and use top to find
              the process causing the spike. If Weblogic or Oracle DB are implicated, there may be underlying hardware or
              configuration issues. Look at historical activity for patterns. Escalate. 
